//NOTE: Comments explain the program without changing its output.
assign count as 10 //TODO: Choose a starting value for your application.

/* A block comment can span
   multiple lines. */
reassign count as count + /* An inline explanation. */ 5

//CRITICAL: Check a result before calling unwrap.
assign parsed as parse_int("42")
if is_ok(parsed) {
    show unwrap(parsed)
}

//FIXME: Replace this demonstration value when adapting the example.
//WARNING: Integer division discards the fractional part.
//HACK: A temporary workaround should explain why it exists.
//DONE: Both line comments and block comments are demonstrated.
/*NOTE: A keyword at the start also colors an entire block comment.
  Block comments end at the first closing marker and do not nest.
*/
show count
show "Comment markers inside strings are text: // and /* ... */"
